// Same self-only `PassWithoutTrace` concealment shape as
// greater_invisibility.ron/invisibility.ron -- the sheet's "controllable
// illusory decoy that moves and speaks" half is dropped, since no
// primitive exists for a player to remote-puppet a second, independently
// visible NPC body (the closest thing, `BasicSummon`, spawns a real
// separate entity with its own AI, not a caster-piloted decoy). Strength
// matched to greater_invisibility.ron (circle 4, one circle below this
// spell) rather than plain invisibility.ron (circle 2) -- both sit well
// above invisibility's own strength, and the detection-multiplier curve's
// diminishing returns (common/src/combat.rs, 1/(1+x)) mean escalating
// further per-circle buys little, so a shared strength across circles 4-5
// is a reasonable plateau, not an oversight.
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.2,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(kind: PassWithoutTrace, data: BuffData(strength: 4.0, duration: Some(60.0))),
    ],
    energy_cost: 90.0,
    meta: (
        school: Some(Illusion),
        source: Some(Arcane),
        // level 5 spell -> min_level 30, the level * 6 convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(30)),
    ),
)
